00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:39.440
very recently viruses became even weirder&nbsp;
when scientists found a completely new type&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:46.960
giant viruses nicknamed gyrus not only did it&nbsp;
break all sorts of records but questioned many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:53.040
assumptions we had about their nature gyruses&nbsp;
even come with their own parasites virophages&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.600 --> 00:03:00.160
viruses that hunt other viruses which seemingly&nbsp;
makes no sense at all and since we identified the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:07.200
first one in 2003 it seems like these giants&nbsp;
are everywhere we look in the oceans in water&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:13.200
towers in the guts of pigs and the mouths of&nbsp;
humans and they're even weirder than we thought&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:19.920
gyruses look funny like hairy geometric&nbsp;
forms or mini pickles much larger than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:25.280
all viruses we knew before which explains how&nbsp;
they could hide in plain sight for centuries&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:29.840
scientists saw them under their microscopes&nbsp;
and just thought they had to be bacteria&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:33.920
it's like suddenly discovering there&nbsp;
are elephant-sized ducks everywhere&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.880 --> 00:03:41.600
most gyruses we've found so far hunt amoebi and&nbsp;
other single-celled beings when they find a victim&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:48.240
they connect with it and use its natural processes&nbsp;
to enter the cell like all viruses their goal is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:55.040
to misappropriate the victim's infrastructure and&nbsp;
procreate imagine a mouse crawling into your mouth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:58.800
and using your guts and bones and&nbsp;
fat tissue to build a mouse factory&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:05.760
the gyrus unloads its attack proteins and genetic&nbsp;
material and rearranges the cell from the inside&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:11.440
its structural elements protein production&nbsp;
machinery and large amounts of mitochondria&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:18.000
for energy are changed to become an actual&nbsp;
factory called viroplasm some gyruses even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:24.080
construct a membrane to shield them from the&nbsp;
cell's antiviral defenses once finished the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:30.080
viroplasm begins to assemble new gyruses using&nbsp;
the victim up from the inside until it's filled up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:37.520
finally the invader usually orders the cell to&nbsp;
self-destruct and releases new gyruses to look&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:44.400
for new prey but what makes gyruses special&nbsp;
is not their modus operandi or their size even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:50.960
it's that they are much more complex than thought&nbsp;
possible for a virus your cells have around 20&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:59.440
000 genes a typical bacterium has a few thousand&nbsp;
genes the coronavirus has around 15 hiv or the flu&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:06.000
around 10. the number of genes alone is certainly&nbsp;
not everything the tomato for example has 35&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:12.960
000 genes but generally we think of life as a&nbsp;
complex system so below a certain complexity level&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.960 --> 00:05:18.160
something may be closer to dead material&nbsp;
rather than a living organism but gyruses&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.160 --> 00:05:24.240
can have hundreds or even thousands of genes&nbsp;
blurring the line between living and dead things&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.280 --> 00:05:31.600
and it's not just the numbers that are special&nbsp;
but also what these genes do we used to think of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:37.200
viral genes as the simplest of instructions just&nbsp;
enough to overcome the defense of their victims&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:44.160
and make new viruses but many gyrus genes&nbsp;
are completely unique basically mystery genes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:50.480
even more confusing a huge selection of their&nbsp;
genes that are actually hallmarks of living&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.480 --> 00:05:57.360
things genes that regulate nutrient intake energy&nbsp;
production light harvesting replication or are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.360 --> 00:06:03.040
just necessary to keep cells alive some recent&nbsp;
studies have even suggested that some gyruses&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.040 --> 00:06:09.200
